sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch08-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The power of natural selection is limited: it can systematically optimize only systems or parts of systems whose behavior is simple, and achieves very little when behavior is complex.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Natural selection works meaningfully only on simple behavior";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 8, “Implications for Everyday Systems”; section “Fundamental Issues in Biology” (from p. 383), p. 392. Scope: natural selection acting on biological traits"
}
